  "described": {
    "alt_text": "A square oil painting on bare wood of a plant made of fat pastel lobes in green, pink, yellow, lilac and orange rising diagonally from the bottom.",
    "description": "A square oil painting on an unprimed wood panel with the grain showing as a warm orange background. A plant of plump rounded lobes climbs from the lower left to the upper right: a sage green lobed trunk at left, lime and yellow arms, a pink arm at centre, lilac and grey lobes above, an orange base at the bottom and a yellow green lobe at right. The lobes are modelled with soft brushwork and pale edges and overlap like stacked pillows. Much of the panel is left as bare wood.",
    "impression": "A cactus that has been upholstered. Leaving the wood bare makes the plant look like it is growing out of a tabletop, and the title admits it is unfinished, which suits it: a plant is always in progress. Soft, warm and a little sleepy.",
